<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<tagGroups>
	<!--
		Human-readable names for the fifth-generation (Halo: Campaign Evolved) tag groups seen in
		real data so far. A CE tag payload only ever states its own group as a four-CC (the
		"group_tag" field of its 64-byte header - see FifthGenTagHeader.GroupTag); there is no
		StringID table for this engine to resolve a description through the way a classic cache
		file's tag group table does (FifthGenGroupInfo.Description is always StringID.Null, by
		design - see that class's remarks), and no embedded English name anywhere in the payload
		itself. A friendly name can only come from outside the format, the same way it already does
		for Halo 1 and Halo 2 Vista below.

		This list is deliberately restricted to groups actually observed in the one real Campaign
		Evolved mod this codebase has been developed and tested against (see
		src/Blamite.Tests/CampaignEvolvedTests.cs) - proj, weap, vehi, scnr - rather than guessed at
		from a classic engine's much larger group table. The four-CCs themselves are not a CE
		invention: every one of them already appears, with this exact spelling and this exact
		English name, in both H1_GroupNames.xml and H2V_GroupNames.xml, which independently agree
		with each other across two different games and roughly a decade. That agreement is the
		basis for reusing the name here rather than guessing - Blam's core tag groups have kept
		their four-CC and their meaning since the original engine, and nothing about the Unreal
		Engine 5 rewrite changes what "weap" or "scnr" identifies. Extend this file as more groups
		are confirmed against real Campaign Evolved data; do not pre-populate it from a classic
		engine's full list on the assumption that every group carried forward unchanged.
	-->
	<group magic="proj" name="projectile" />
	<group magic="scnr" name="scenario" />
	<group magic="vehi" name="vehicle" />
	<group magic="weap" name="weapon" />
</tagGroups>
